  "name": "doi-10-5281-zenodo-19476542",
  "notes": "Op^3 (pronounced O-p-cubed) is an integrated numerical modeling framework for offshore wind turbines that connects OptumGX 3D FE limit analysis, OpenSeesPy 1D beam-on-nonlinear-Winkler-foundation structural dynamics, and OpenFAST aero-hydro-servo-elastic whole-turbine simulation into a single verifiable pipeline. Developed around the Gunsan 4.2 MW tripod suction bucket offshore wind turbine and benchmarked against the complete NREL reference wind turbine library. Offers four selectable foundation modules in OpenSeesPy (fixed, 6x6 lumped stiffness, distributed BNWF springs, dissipation-weighted generalized BNWF) and a direct bridge to OpenFAST SubDyn for aero-hydro-servo-elastic coupling.",
